---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import InlineIcon from '../../components/InlineIcon.astro';
import JsonLd from '../../components/JsonLd.astro';
import PogoRoute from '../../components/work/PogoRoute.astro';
import { POGO } from '../../data/work';
---
<BaseLayout title="Pogo · Rishi Ahuja" description={POGO.description} cover="blue">
  <JsonLd data={{ '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'SoftwareSourceCode', name: POGO.name, description: POGO.description, url: new URL(POGO.path, Astro.site).href, codeRepository: POGO.repository, license: `${POGO.repository}/blob/main/LICENSE`, author: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'Rishi Ahuja', url: new URL('/', Astro.site).href } }} />
  <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
    <section class="pogo-hero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }]} />
        <div class="pogo-intro">
          <div><h1>Pogo</h1><p class="pogo-tagline">The scenic route<br class="desktop-break" /> to your cluster.</p></div>
          <div class="pogo-hero-copy">
            <p>A spare laptop stays on campus. You take yours with you. Pogo keeps a route back to the compute cluster, through a reverse SSH tunnel that can recover when the connection drops.</p>
            <a class="button" href={POGO.repository} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Source code <InlineIcon name="arrow-up-right" /></a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <PogoRoute />
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="pogo-story wrap" aria-labelledby="pogo-story-title">
      <h2 id="pogo-story-title">Campus compute,<br /> from wherever I am.</h2>
      <div class="pogo-prose">
        <p>The university’s compute cluster is available from the campus network. That is inconvenient when an experiment is still running and I’m somewhere else.</p>
        <p>I built Pogo around a spare laptop that could stay on campus. It keeps a way back to the cluster open, so I can check jobs, collect results, or submit the next run from my own laptop.</p>
        <p>Pogo also helps the connection recover when campus Wi-Fi drops. Less time tending a connection, more time getting back to the experiment.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .pogo-hero { background: var(--cover-blue); padding: 1.5rem 0 2.5rem; }
  .pogo-intro { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1.1fr) minmax(0,1fr); gap: 5rem; align-items: center; margin-top: 2.6rem; }
  .pogo-intro h1 { margin: 0; font-size: clamp(4.4rem,7.5vw,7rem); font-weight: 500; line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -0.055em; }
  .pogo-tagline { margin: 0.6rem 0 0; font-size: clamp(1.65rem,2.6vw,2.75rem); line-height: 1.2; letter-spacing: -0.025em; }
  .pogo-hero-copy p { margin: 0; max-width: 32em; font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  .pogo-hero-copy .button { margin-top: 1.5rem; font-size: 0.78rem; }
  .pogo-story { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0,0.9fr) minmax(0,1.1fr); gap: 4rem; padding-block: 4rem; }
  .pogo-story h2 { margin: 0; font-size: clamp(1.5rem,2.4vw,2.35rem); line-height: 1.25; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -0.025em; }
  .pogo-prose p { margin: 0; }
  .pogo-prose p + p { margin-top: 1rem; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .pogo-hero { padding-top: 1rem; padding-bottom: 2rem; }
    .pogo-intro { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; margin-top: 1.75rem; }
    .pogo-intro h1 { font-size: 4.5rem; }
    .pogo-tagline { font-size: 1.8rem; }
    .desktop-break { display: none; }
    .pogo-hero-copy p { font-size: 1rem; }
    .pogo-story { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.25rem; padding-block: 2.8rem; }
  }
</style>
